+# AKS Price List Module: integration guide
+
+This module is **additive**. It does not replace or modify the 3F Excel controller.
+
+## Source changes
+
+- `client/src/features/prices/aks/{AksPricePage,ImportAksDialog,types}.tsx` (types is `.ts`) — new UI, multiple-PDF upload, preview, search and infinite scroll.
+- `client/src/app/App.tsx` — adds the protected `/price-list/aks` route.
+- `client/src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx` — adds AKS submenu.
+- `server/src/features/prices/aks/{routes,parser,lineParser}.ts` — separate API and PDF extractor.
+- `server/src/index.ts` — mounts AKS API under `/api/price-lists/aks`.
+- `server/sql/aks.sql` — production migration for phpMyAdmin; `schema.sql` is updated for new local databases.
+- `server/package.json` — `pdfjs-dist@4.10.38` (Node 20 compatible).
+
+## Local setup (Windows)
+
+From project root:
+
+```powershell
+npm install pdfjs-dist@4.10.38 -w server
+npm run db:setup
+npm run test:aks
+npm run check:aks -- "C:\\path\\to\\AKS-quote.pdf"
+npm run typecheck
+npm run build
+npm run dev
+```
+
+`npm install` regenerates the root `package-lock.json` — commit BOTH that lockfile and `server/package.json`, otherwise GitHub Actions `npm ci` will fail.
+
+## cPanel setup without terminal
+
+1. In **cPanel > phpMyAdmin**, choose the existing Sales Portal database and **Import** `server/sql/aks.sql`. Do not re-import the entire schema if you already have users and 3F data.
+2. On your PC, commit the new code, `server/package.json` and updated `package-lock.json`, and push to `main`. Existing GitHub Actions uploads compiled code to `/api`.
+3. After deployment, open **cPanel > Setup Node.js App**, run **NPM Install** for the API (new `pdfjs-dist` dependency), then restart the app. Keep `app.cjs` as the working Passenger startup file; do not overwrite it.
+4. Open `/price-list/aks`. Users need `prices:read` to view and `prices:upload` to upload. Super admin already bypasses individual permission checks.
+
+## API endpoints
+
+All require an authenticated session:
+
+- `GET /api/price-lists/aks/meta` — current AKS imported batch and its file metadata.
+- `GET /api/price-lists/aks/items?q=&sourceFile=&page=1&limit=20` — paginated search.
+- `POST /api/price-lists/aks/preview` — multipart form with `files` repeated, **1–8 PDFs**.
+- `POST /api/price-lists/aks/import` — same multipart form; atomically replaces current AKS records.
+
+## Import policy
+
+- Up to 8 PDF files, 8 MB each, 32 MB combined, 50 pages per PDF.
+- PDFs must contain selectable text and AKS quotation table columns `Part No.`, `Description`, `Price`, `UOM`, `MOQ QTY`. Scans require future OCR support.
+- Uses AUD. Stores quote reference, quote date, expiration when explicitly given, original PDF filename/page, prices, UOM and MOQ. Only extracted data and source filenames are saved in MySQL; original PDF binaries are not permanently stored.
+- Fails closed for unreadable files, detectable unparsed product rows and duplicate part numbers across the batch. Correct these and preview again.
+- Deleting and replacing AKS prices happens inside one transaction **only after every input file has parsed successfully**; the previous list is restored if the insert fails.
+- Never touches 3F tables/data, except adding `aks` to the shared `price_suppliers` reference table.
+- Preview returns the first 60 extracted rows; the actual import processes *all* rows.
+
+## Important limitation
+
+The PDF parser is tailored to the **supplied AKS quotation layout**. Some future quotations may use other formats. Test those in preview first. The extracted sample quotation dated 26 May 2026 indicates 30-day validity and is already expired.
+
+## Testing status
+
+The 9 rows from the uploaded quotation were verified with the row parser and a text-position simulation based on the actual PDF page. Full `npm install` / TypeScript and browser integration could not be performed in this environment. Run the provided commands locally before deploying.
